This program is designed to encode and decode text using Python’s Base64 plugin. Encoding is the process of converting readable data into a different format that can be safely stored and or transmitted. 
Decoding, on the other hand, converts the encoded data back into its original form. My program allows users to enter text, choose whether they want to encode or decode whatever they would like (images coming soon)
as long as its base64.  

Challenges:

My main challenge was developing the image decoder as writting the program wasn't the hard part, it was finding a way to display the image after decoding it.
eventually research lead me down a rabit whole where i was faced with 2 ultimatetums; use tkinter to display the image or use a different plugin; the os plugin
which handles Miscellaneous operating system interfaces. Ultimately I went with the ladder, as albiet I am familiar with Tkinter I wanted to try something new, 
and after doing a fair share of research I found that this method was actually easier and faster than the Tkinter method as I only needed to utilize 1 command
to acomplish my goal. Both encountering and conquering this obstacle allowed me to discover a new plugin and learn more commands, and tools that I could possibly 
in other projects.

